     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><br></p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;border-left:4px solid rgb(221,221,221);padding:0px 1em;color:rgb(119,119,119);quotes:none\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">‘They’ did write documentation that told you that Perl was needed, but ‘they’ can’t read it for you. <br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">   — Brian D. Ripley <br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">      R-help (February 2001)</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This was documented in vignettes. I will not answer here and leave it for you to <strong>read</strong> the vignettes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Fri, Feb 17, 2017 at 12:50 AM, Vijay Ramesh &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vjj...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<div><br></div><div>Is there an option to plot only the clade chosen when I use the groupClade function on a particular node number?</div><div><br></div><div><div>node6580 &lt;- groupClade(new tree, node = 6580, group_name = &quot;6580&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>ggtree(node6580, aes(color=group, linetype=group), layout = &quot;circular&quot;) + geom_tiplab2(size=0.1, color=&quot;purple&quot;) #This ends up plotting the entire tree, and highlighting that clade along with the rest. </div></div><div><br></div><div>I would like to extract only that subclade.</div><div><br></div><div>Any thoughts?<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div><div>Vijay</div><div><br></div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br>\r\